# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Keeps the build context small and, more importantly, keeps host-built
# artefacts out of the image. A host `node_modules` copied into a Linux image is
# the classic source of "works locally, crashes in the container": native
# binaries (bcrypt, esbuild, Prisma engines) are platform-specific.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage

# Generated by `prisma generate` inside the image.
server/src/generated

# Secrets are supplied at run time via `env_file`, never baked into a layer.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

**/*.log
.git
.github
.vscode
.idea
.vercel
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# The API image does not serve the SPA — Vercel builds `web/` separately. But
# npm refuses to resolve a workspace tree with a missing member manifest, so
# `web/package.json` has to remain visible to `npm ci`.
web/*
!web/package.json

# Scratch files from local verification runs.
**/*.tmp.mjs
**/*.tmp.ts
README.md
docker-compose.yml
